      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg per day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for prescriptions is **3200 mg/day** (for example, 800 mg four times daily).\n- This order is twice the single-dose maximum and twice the daily maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and other toxicity, even in a patient with normal organ function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common mix-up where the daily total is written as the per-dose amount.\n2. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum prescription dose).\n3. **800 mg three times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, say so explicitly and give a short reason, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
