       "text": "I entered the order as written. **Order ID: ORD-0001** is ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth, four times daily (6400 mg/day total).\n\nYou didn't give a clinical reason, so the order note says:\n- The dose is above the usual maximums of 800 mg per dose and 3200 mg/day.\n- You were told this and confirmed the order as written, with no reason given.\n- A pharmacist needs to check it before it's dispensed.\n\nAt this dose, it would be wise to:\n- Consider GI protection, such as a proton pump inhibitor.\n- Check kidney function and electrolytes, and watch for bleeding.\n- Avoid giving other NSAIDs, anticoagulants or steroids at the same time unless that's intended.\n\nIf you want to add the clinical reason to the order, change the dose, or set a stop date, I can do that."
